<launch>

  <!--
    Team Xiao Hei AI module — entry point.

    The package name and this file's name are kept from the challenge template
    so the evaluation's `ros2 launch dummy_vlm dummy_vlm.launch` still works.

    Only one process starts here: the router. It waits for
    /challenge_question, decides which of the three question types arrived,
    and then either

      instruction-following  -> drives the route itself (VLM grounding +
                                lidar lift + waypoints), in this process;
      numerical              -> answers in this process too;
      object reference       -> hands the process over to one of two
                                perception-backed pipelines, chosen by
                                XIAO_HEI_REFERENCE_LAUNCH:
                                  scene_gemini.launch  frontier sweep, then
                                                       Gemini answers (default)
                                  scene_claude.launch  nav_task1 drives at the
                                                       named object, then
                                                       Claude answers

    One process at a time, by construction: the hand-off `exec`s. That matters
    because the frontier explorer publishes waypoints from the moment it
    starts, and two things steering /way_point_with_heading is not a race we
    would win.

    Configuration is by environment variable — ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (required),
    XIAO_HEI_CLASSIFY, XIAO_HEI_BUDGET_S, XIAO_HEI_IMAGE_TOPIC. See
    ai_module/README.md.
  -->
  <node pkg="dummy_vlm" exec="dummyVLM" name="dummyVLM" output="screen" />

</launch>
